        <mxCell id="oSQ-Hx1KtzNKTa1L_6uN-1" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;displaying an attached html file&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="230" y="30" width="300" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oSQ-Hx1KtzNKTa1L_6uN-3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;A html file is a (formatted) text file that&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;contains marked up text.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;The mark up is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;recognized by (web) browsers, and the marked-up content is rendered by the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;browser as the markup directs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;When an email has an attached html file, the procedure for displaying the file content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;depends on the application which handles your emails and your operating system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Big help huh? Well, if your email reader is configured for it, opening it might display it in the browser given it&#39;s html extension. My email reader is not that smart. I must download it and then open it. Maybe the diagram helps a bit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
